# ── Facts for writing the post ──────────────────────────────
# Raw material, not copy. Shown on /studio/downloads/ so the post can be
# written on a phone without switching back to a laptop to look something
# up. Every line here is checked against the site or src/_data — a line
# starting "ASK:" is a gap only Terry or Dalton can fill.
#
# Keep this list true. It is the thing someone will trust at 6am.
facts:
  - group: "The people — lead with this"
    items:
      - "Terry Booker and Dalton Watkins, business partners, are the two names on the door."
      - "This post gets shared by friends and family first. They recognise a name long before an address, so open on the people, not the premises."
      - "ASK: how long has each of them been cooking, and where?"
      - "ASK: how did the two of them come to be partners?"
      - "ASK: who runs which side day to day — kitchen, catering, front of house?"
      - "ASK: what does reopening the dining room actually mean to them, in their own words? One sentence in Terry's voice beats a paragraph in ours."
      - "ASK: one specific thing — a dish one of them is known for, a habit, something they always say. Specifics are what get shared; adjectives are not."
      - "NEEDED: a photo of the two of them, in the kitchen or at the door. It would out-perform this graphic. None exists, and AI imagery is off the table — so the graphic is what ships, and a photo is worth taking before the next post."

  - group: "The date and the practical facts"
    items:
      - "Opening Monday, October 5th, 2026."
      - "Hours 6:00am to 2:00pm, Monday through Friday."
      - "417 S 6th St, Leavenworth, KS 66048."
      - "Phone (913) 547-9994."
      - "lvcafetogo.com and facebook.com/LVCafeToGo."
      - "It is an opening, not a grand opening — the menu is brand new and needs time to settle. The celebration comes later."

  - group: "How it will actually run"
    items:
      - "Order and go. Seating is available, but there is no table service."
      - "Deli-style menu — no fried foods. The tri-fold in this studio still lists fried potatoes and chips; it predates this decision and needs a pass."
      - "Limited beverage options."
      - "The menu is still being adjusted through September. Some old favourites return, some new items get tried."
      - "Catering by email: theabcafe@gmail.com."

  - group: "The history"
    items:
      - "Opened 2005 — twenty-one years — serving Leavenworth County."
      - "Went private in 2015 to serve Meals on Wheels alongside the Council on Aging, and focused on catering."
      - "Has catered the Lansing Lions and Rotary, and events at the Leavenworth Community Center. Named groups are worth naming — they are the people most likely to share the post."
      - "Started in the historic Abernathy Building, near the Centennial Bridge, as a weekday breakfast-and-lunch counter."
      - "Daily specials, sandwiches made to order, soups, salads, home-style plates."
      - "Moved locations several times around Leavenworth over the years."
      - "October 5th is the return to serving the public directly. Do NOT say we are back in the Abernathy Building — that is where it started, not where it is."

  - group: "The food"
    items:
      - "ASK: the deli-style, no-fried-foods decision changes the menu. Which items survive, and which come off? Everything below is the old list."
      - "Breakfast: biscuits and gravy full or half, the Big Breakfast, burritos, 2/3 egg omelets, breakfast sandwiches. Burritos and omelets are build-your-own."
      - "Lunch: wraps, sandwiches, burgers and chicken — Navajo burger, patty melt, Philly steak, Reuben, clubhouse. Salads full or half, soup of the day, sides."
      - "Breakfast runs about $5 to $11, lunch mostly $8 to $12."
      - "Catering is not going anywhere: sit-down dinners with china and linen, buffets, drop-off, appetizer and station service. Fifteen guest minimum, dietary accommodations on request."

  - group: "How to end it"
    items:
      - "Ask a question. A cold page lives on comments, and comments are reach."
      - "Best one: what do you want to see on the menu? The menu is genuinely still being written, so the answer changes something."
      - "Ask people to share it. For a reopening, that is the whole distribution plan."

  - group: "Do not say"
    items:
      - "Naming Meals on Wheels and the Council on Aging as history is fine — that is our own record. The bid, who won it, and per-meal pricing are not."
      - "Not 'grand opening'."
      - "Nothing we have not checked. A wrong hour or a wrong price on a post that gets shared is the expensive kind of mistake."

